  "definition": "The reliability index typically ranges from 0 to 1, where values below 0.5 indicate equipment that fails frequently and requires constant maintenance, values between 0.5-0.8 represent equipment with occasional failures that require regular maintenance, and values above 0.8 indicate highly reliable equipment with minimal downtime."
}

